{"info":{"author":"Anki Team","author_email":null,"bugtrack_url":null,"classifiers":[],"description":"# aqt — Anki Qt GUI\n\n`aqt` is the Qt-based desktop interface for [Anki](https://apps.ankiweb.net), the spaced repetition flashcard program.\n\nIt provides all the visual components of the Anki desktop app: the deck browser, card editor, reviewer, browser, add-on manager, and more. Under the hood it uses PyQt6 and communicates with Anki's core logic via the [`anki`](https://pypi.org/project/anki/) package.\n\n## Running\n\nOnce installed, Anki can be launched from the command line:\n\n```bash\nanki\n```\n\n## Add-on development\n\nIf you are building an Anki add-on, this is the package that exposes the GUI hooks and Qt widgets you need. See the [Add-on Guide](https://addon-docs.ankiweb.net/) for full documentation.\n\n## Source code\n\n<https://github.com/ankitects/anki>\n","description_content_type":"text/markdown","docs_url":null,"download_url":null,"downloads":{"last_day":-1,"last_month":-1,"last_week":-1},"dynamic":null,"home_page":null,"keywords":null,"license":null,"license_expression":"AGPL-3.0-or-later","license_files":null,"maintainer":null,"maintainer_email":null,"name":"aqt","package_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aqt/","platform":null,"project_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aqt/","project_urls":{"Bug Tracker":"https://github.com/ankitects/anki/issues","Source Code":"https://github.com/ankitects/anki","homepage":"https://github.com/ankitects/anki"},"provides_extra":["audio","qt","qt610","qt68","qt69"],"release_url":"https://pypi.org/project/aqt/26.9.3/","requires_dist":["anki-mac-helper>=0.1.1; sys_platform == \"darwin\"","beautifulsoup4","flask[async]","jsonschema","packaging","pyqt6-webengine>=6.2","pyqt6>=6.2","pywin32; sys_platform == \"win32\"","requests","send2trash","truststore>=0.10.4","waitress>=2.0.0","anki==26.09.3","anki-audio==0.2.3; (sys_platform == \"win32\" or sys_platform == \"darwin\") and extra == \"audio\"","pyqt6-qt6==6.11.2; extra =